Algorithm 2: localSearch (R(U))
1: $R_{ls} = len\_R(U)^{*0.15}; \% len\_R(U)$ : the size of R(U)
2: For i = 1: $R_{ls}$ Do
3: $R_{1} \leftarrow R(U)(i)$ ;
4: Chrom_all $\leftarrow R_{1}$ .chromosome;
5: find the critical operations $C_{op}$ and blocks $C_{b}$ of R1;
6: If rand < 0.5 Then
7: execute Algorithm 3 for OS vector to generate $R_{2}$ ;
8: Else
9: execute Algorithm 4 for MA vector to generate $R_{2}$ ;
10: End If
11: $R(U)(i) \leftarrow R_{2}$ ;
12: End For
13: $R'(U) \leftarrow R(U)$ ;
14: Return (R'(U))

Algorithm 3: localsearchOS ( $R_{1}$ , Chrom_all, $C_{op}$ )

1: generate randomly two unequal positions ( $P_{1}$ (small), $P_{2}$ (large)) from 1 to the length of $C_{op}$ 2: Chrom_os ← Chrom_all(1, :);

3: swap the genes between position $P_{1}$ and position $P_{2}$ on Chrom_os to form Chrom_new;

4: Chrom_new(2:3, :) ← Chrom_all(2:3, :);

5: decode Chrom_new to form R_new;

6: If R_new dominates $R_{1}$ Then $R_{2}$ ← R_new; Else $R_{2}$ ← $R_{1}$ ;

End If

7: Return ( $R_{2}$ )

Algorithm 4: localsearchMA ( $R_{1}$ , Chrom_all, $C_{b}$ )

1: If isempty ( $C_{b}$ ) Then
2:    back to execute Algorithm 3 for OS vector;
3: Else
4:    Chrom_fama ← Chrom_all(2:3, :);
5:    generate randomly an integer $P_{3}$ from 1 to the size of $C_{b}$ ;
6:    block_1 ← $C_{b}(P_{3})$ ;
7:    generate randomly a position ( $P_{4}$ ) between 1 and the length of block_1 and identify the operation ope_rank of $P_{4}$ on block_1;
8:    find the ope_rank on Chrom_fama, mark the corresponding position as $P_{5}$ , and extract the fa_rank and ma_rank of the ope_rank;
9:    If rand < 0.5 Then %perform the LSO_MPT for MA vector
10:    find all available machines of the operation ope_rank and select the machine ma_new and corresponding factory fa_new with minimum processing time except fa_rank and ma_rank;
11:    Chrom_fama(2:3, $P_{5}$ ) ← [fa_new; ma_new];
12:    Else %perform the LSO_RTT for MA vector
13:    find fa_pre and ma_pre of the precedent operation of the ope_rank;
14:    If isempty(ma_pre) Then
15:    find all available machines of the ope_rank and select the machine ma_new and corresponding factory fa_new with shortest processing time except fa_rank and ma_rank;
16:    Chrom_fama(2:3, $P_{5}$ ) ← [fa_new; ma_new];
17:    Else
18:    Select a machine ma_new and corresponding factory fa_new trying to keep in line with fa_pre and ma_pre from all available machines of the ope_rank;
19:    Chrom_fama(2:3, $P_{5}$ ) ← [fa_new; ma_new];
20:    End If
21:    End If
22: End If
23: Chrom_one ← Chrom_fama(2:3, :); Chrom_one ← Chrom_all (1, :);

